WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations on
your Academy Award nomination.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very exciting.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's such a blessing, man.
I mean, ooh!

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.875 size:81% position:41%
-My mother said, like,
"Can you believe it?

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
A little black boy
from the South Side of Chicago

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.013 line:92%
is nominated for an Oscar?"

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:15.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Man.
That is an amazing journey.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.416 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great. And it's not
happening on its own.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were also nominated
for a Grammy.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you were there last Sunday?
How was that?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.893
Did you -- Are you nervous on
a day where you're nominated?

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah.
You know, it's, like,

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:32.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
unfortunately and fortunately,
they announced our award

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
pre-telecast,
so we already knew we lost.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.971
We lost, so -- so I kind of got
to enjoy the event.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.940 size:88% position:44%
Like, I mean, I saw this
incredible performance

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
by Kendrick Lamar.
-It's amazing.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.544 line:92%
-You know, it was beautiful.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even watching Bruno Mars
and Cardi B was fun.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just seeing
Jay-Z and the guys

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.888
that I really love and care
about as artists and as people,

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.991
like Naz and Jay-Z around,
just enjoying the Grammys.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:58.525 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was fun.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I -- It was another one of
those moments,

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.161 size:81% position:41% line:92%
because I pulled up --

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I pulled up to
Madison Square Garden

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.398
I was thinking, like, "I used to
watch the Grammys.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.232 line:92%
I used to see Michael Jackson

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:08.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
and never think that I could
attend that event."

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I mean?
-Yeah.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.603 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Yeah, it's incredible.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's incred-- I mean,
just the fact that

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're having all of these
happening one after the other.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:16.476
It's like, "I'm at the Grammys.
I'm at the Oscars."

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:17.177 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's really exciting.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:20.113
You know, you talked about
the people from your era,

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
the guys you came up with,
Jay-Z and Naz.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.716 line:92%
I always love hearing when

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
people help out
younger, unknown artists.

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you --
This was a photo you posted

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
of you and Chance the Rapper
when he was in "SNL."

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.725
He looks a lot older there
than he does in real life.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:36.563
He's actually younger than you.
-Yeah, just a little bit. Yeah.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.764 line:92%
-But you -- Is it true that

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
your grandmother and Chance's
grandmother are friends?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.969 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah. Well, yeah.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.137 line:92%
They are -- they were friends --

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll say that because Chance's
grandmother has passed,

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
God bless her soul.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.877 size:88% position:44%
But, so, my grandmother
and Chance's grandmother

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.813
were friends, and my grandmother
said, "Hey, Rashid,

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:56.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need you to call
and leave a message.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
My friend's grandson,
he's a rapper."

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is -- this is like
10 years ago.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.189 size:78% position:39%
So Chance had to be,
like, in high school.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.190 line:92%
So I ended up calling him.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to do what
your grandmother says.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, of course.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I -- you know,
and my grandmother

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.364 line:92%
is known for calling me, saying,

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Say hi to this person.
Do this."

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:14.501 line:92%
So I had to do it. I called --

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's very nice that you still
answer when she calls.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's very nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.007 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I better.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah.
I called Chance's phone.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.777 size:75% position:38%
I didn't know he was
Chance the Rapper.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.146 line:92%
At that point I don't even know

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
if his name was
Chance the Rapper.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.750
But I left a message for him.
He didn't answer the call.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I left a message,
an inspirational message

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.722
telling him to pursue his dream
and do it.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I met him
eight years later.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, you know,
"Our grandmothers are friends

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you left a message
on my phone.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.496 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'll never forget that."

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "What?"
-Wow.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"That was you?"
That was incredible.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this dude went on
to win Grammys

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be one of the biggest
rappers out there.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.570 line:92%
-Well, good for you, man.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.371 line:92%
That is such a nice thing --

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
such a nice way
to pay it forward like that.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.340 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's great.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Would you do that for
an up and coming comedian?

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.012 line:92%
I can't stress how busy I am.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just -- I just don't
have the time.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.451
And then, you know, I'm on
a very limited minutes plan.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to talk about
"The Chi."

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.657
This is a fantastic show that
was created by Lena Waithe,

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:13.726
who's an Emmy Award-winning
writer on "Master of None."

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how did this show
come to be?

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:16.629 size:81% position:41% line:92%
How did it come about?

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, she created it
because she said,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
she saw a lot of reports
about Chicago

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:25.505
and the statistics that was
happening with the murder rates.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.207 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And she realized that

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
people weren't looking at us
as human beings.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:33.279
The life that was being talked
about was not looked at as like,

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
oh, these are
human beings dying.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:38.651
And this is not only the side of
what Chicago is, is violence.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it sparked a thought
in her mind.

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's a creative person,
beautiful writer.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:45.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she wrote the pilot for
"The Chi."

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:49.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as producers,
Freedom Road and my company,

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.431 line:92%
we heard about the script.

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.699 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It had a real big buzz.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.633 line:92%
And we came on as producers.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:57.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was like -- It was just
the right alignment for me,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.304 size:81% position:41% line:92%
me being from Chicago.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
Me always wanting to tell that
story about human life

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:04.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just life being round,
not just one-sided.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what
she was able to show.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:08.748
-It's wonderful. You're --
obviously, we saw from the clip.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.449 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You're in it as well.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you decide to be in
a project like this,

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:14.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you go at it
with a very specific,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I want to play a character
like this"?

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:17.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or "I want to bring
this experience,

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:18.558 size:81% position:41% line:92%
either my own personal

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
or people I knew
from that part of the country"

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe other people don't
know that much about?

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, yeah.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.431 line:92%
You know, they said, you know,

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you want to do
a character on it?

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Yeah,
if the character is right."

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they wrote this character
named Rafik,

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.740 size:88% position:44%
who was a Muslim brother
who was from the streets

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.843
and then, you know, went to
prison and has changed his life.

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:39.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I really definitely know
human beings

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:40.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
who have been
through that transition.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:44.717
In fact, I've been working with
something called Imagine Justice

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:45.518 size:88% position:44% line:92%
where we go into prisons

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.655 size:88% position:44%
and talk to individuals
and see what programs --

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:49.355 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I've met some of

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.457 size:84% position:42%
the most enlightened
human beings in prison.

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.961
So, to be able to play this
character and just be a voice

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:57.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
for people who are
usually unheard

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.031 line:92%
was really an honor for me.

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:01.668
You know, I'm super grateful to
be a part of it as a producer.

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:03.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also to be
a voice for the people

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
who, across all America,
who don't usually get heard.

